a causeway across the bay connects  Markin to the mainland the sleepy island  is just 45 minutes from Amsterdam the  lighthouse has been keeping sailors on  course for more than 170 years Liliana  and ties spyker have been living in the  lighthouse Alex for 12 years now they  renovated it from the ground up turning  it into their dream home oh I was a  sailor before so I like the water in the  ship's and now I live in the water with  the ships around look around it's the  freedom its water it's nice weather and  of course also sometimes dead weather  that's why we love living me living in  the lighthouse they have 90 square  meters of living space over two levels  and everywhere that collection of naval  memorabilia reminds them of their great  passion the ocean  everything what happened with water and  chips and lighthouses I collect that's a  small small tick I make a special corner  my wife it's not amused with it I have  to clean it is easier that you were  coiler that's it a narrow spiral  staircase winds 15 meters of the tower  in years gone by it was manned by a  lighthouse keeper today the signal  beacon operates automatically but ty  spyker does carry out mine repairs and  he's added a few conveniences IV put  officiated on the under delight with a  few beers and a bottle of wine and a few  stairs with NH three beers you have to  go to the toilet so you could better sit  down stairs of a QB than upstairs not  everything has been fully modernized  though electricity is produced by a  generator about 200 meters away  it's peaceful and scenic with water as  far as the eye can see tap water comes  from tanks that need to be refilled with  water from the village once a month but  they've learned to live with the small  inconveniences well you have to be more  efficient you don't throw away it you  don't leave the tip open when you were  brushing your teeth the Spikers pay a  monthly rent of about 500 euros the  closest supermarket is two kilometers  away but they don't mind the isolation  we're not lonesome I think loneliness  you also do a lot by yourself if you  don't accept people if you don't talk to  people if you don't do anything to have  companion then you're lonely but no we  have a lot of friends we have a lot of  guests a lot of visitors  whatever the inconveniences they still  have what makes the most happy all  around them the sea for Liliana and ties  spyker living in a lighthouse is a dream  come true
 

